+.. _device-modules:
+
+========================================
+QEMU Device Modules (External Devices)
+========================================
+
+Overview
+========
+
+QEMU supports loading device models as dynamically loaded shared libraries.
+This allows developers to create custom device models without modifying or
+recompiling QEMU itself.

+
+Device modules use the same QOM (QEMU Object Model) and QDEV APIs as
+built-in devices, but are compiled separately and loaded at runtime.
+
+Use Cases
+=========
+
+Device modules are useful for:
+
+- **Custom hardware modeling**: Model proprietary or specialized hardware
+- **Rapid prototyping**: Quickly iterate on device designs
+- **Educational purposes**: Teaching hardware/software interfaces
+- **Proprietary IP**: Distribute device models without source code
+- **Legacy hardware**: Model discontinued or niche hardware
+
+Prerequisites
+=============
+
+To build device modules, you need:
+
+1. **QEMU Device SDK**: Headers and configuration files
+
+   - Install via package manager (e.g., ``qemu-device-sdk`` package)
+   - Or use ``make install-dev-sdk`` when building QEMU from source
+
+2. **Development tools**:
+
+   - C compiler (GCC or Clang)
+   - GLib development files (``glib-2.0-dev`` or ``glib2-devel``)
+   - pkg-config tool
+
+3. **QEMU with module support**: Ensure QEMU was built with ``--enable-modules``
+
+Quick Start
+===========
+
+Minimal Device Module
+---------------------
+
+Here's a minimal SysBus device module::
+
+    /* minimal-device.c */
+    #define BUILD_DSO
+    #include "qemu/osdep.h"
+    #include "qemu/module.h"
+    #include "hw/sysbus.h"
+    #include "qom/object.h"
+
+    #define TYPE_MINIMAL_DEVICE "minimal-device"
+    OBJECT_DECLARE_SIMPLE_TYPE(MinimalDeviceState, MINIMAL_DEVICE)
+
+    struct MinimalDeviceState {
+        SysBusDevice parent_obj;
+        MemoryRegion mmio;
+    };
+
+    static uint64_t minimal_device_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, unsigned size)
+    {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    static void minimal_device_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr,
+                                    uint64_t val, unsigned size)
+    {
+    }
+
+    static const MemoryRegionOps minimal_device_ops = {
+        .read = minimal_device_read,
+        .write = minimal_device_write,
+        .endianness = DEVICE_NATIVE_ENDIAN,
+    };
+
+    static void minimal_device_init(Object *obj)
+    {
+        MinimalDeviceState *s = MINIMAL_DEVICE(obj);
+        SysBusDevice *sbd = SYS_BUS_DEVICE(obj);
+        
+        memory_region_init_io(&s->mmio, obj, &minimal_device_ops, s,
+                            TYPE_MINIMAL_DEVICE, 0x1000);
+        sysbus_init_mmio(sbd, &s->mmio);
+    }
+
+    static void minimal_device_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, const void *data)
+    {
+        DeviceClass *dc = DEVICE_CLASS(oc);
+        dc->desc = "Minimal Example Device";
+    }
+
+    static const TypeInfo minimal_device_info = {
+        .name          = TYPE_MINIMAL_DEVICE,
+        .parent        = TYPE_SYS_BUS_DEVICE,
+        .instance_size = sizeof(MinimalDeviceState),
+        .instance_init = minimal_device_init,
+        .class_init    = minimal_device_class_init,
+    };
+
+    static void minimal_device_register_types(void)
+    {
+        type_register_static(&minimal_device_info);
+    }
+
+    type_init(minimal_device_register_types)
+    module_obj(TYPE_MINIMAL_DEVICE);
+
+Building the Module
+-------------------
+
+Using pkg-config::
+
+    gcc $(pkg-config --cflags qemu-device) \\
+        -fPIC -shared minimal-device.c \\
+        -o hw-minimal-device.so \\
+        $(pkg-config --libs glib-2.0)
+
+Or with explicit paths::
+
+    gcc -I/usr/include/qemu-device \\
+        -I/usr/include/qemu-device/config \\
+        -DBUILD_DSO \\
+        $(pkg-config --cflags glib-2.0) \\
+        -fPIC -shared minimal-device.c \\
+        -o hw-minimal-device.so \\
+        $(pkg-config --libs glib-2.0)
+
+Using the Module
+----------------
+
+1. Place the module where QEMU can find it::
+
+       export QEMU_MODULE_DIR=/path/to/modules
+       cp hw-minimal-device.so $QEMU_MODULE_DIR/
+
+2. Use the device in QEMU::
+
+       qemu-system-x86_64 -M pc -device minimal-device
+
+QEMU will automatically load ``hw-minimal-device.so`` when you specify
+``-device minimal-device``.
+
+Module Naming Convention
+========================
+
+Module filenames must follow this pattern::
+
+    hw-<typename>.so       # Linux/Unix
+    hw-<typename>.dll      # Windows  
+    hw-<typename>.dylib    # macOS
+
+For example, a device with ``TYPE_MY_UART`` → ``hw-my-uart.so``
+
+Required Module Symbols
+=======================
+
+Every device module must:
+
+1. Define ``BUILD_DSO`` before including headers
+2. Include ``qemu/module.h``
+3. Use ``type_init()`` macro to register device types
+4. Use ``module_obj()`` macro to declare exported types
+5. Implement ``qemu_module_dummy()`` (automatically added by headers)
+
+Device Types
+============
+
+SysBus Devices
+--------------
+
+For memory-mapped devices on the system bus::
+
+    #include "hw/sysbus.h"
+    
+    .parent = TYPE_SYS_BUS_DEVICE
+
+PCI Devices
+-----------
+
+For PCI devices::
+
+    #include "hw/pci/pci.h"
+    
+    .parent = TYPE_PCI_DEVICE
+    .interfaces = (const InterfaceInfo[]) {
+        { INTERFACE_CONVENTIONAL_PCI_DEVICE },
+        { },
+    }
+
+ISA Devices
+-----------
+
+For ISA bus devices::
+
+    #include "hw/isa/isa.h"
+    
+    .parent = TYPE_ISA_DEVICE
+
+USB Devices
+-----------
+
+For USB devices::
+
+    #include "hw/usb.h"
+    
+    .parent = TYPE_USB_DEVICE
+
+API Stability
+=============
+
+Stable APIs (Safe to use)
+--------------------------
+
+These APIs are considered stable within QEMU major versions:
+
+- QOM core: ``object_new()``, ``object_class_by_name()``, type registration
+- QDEV core: ``DeviceClass``, ``DeviceState``, ``realize``/``unrealize``
+- Memory regions: ``MemoryRegion``, ``MemoryRegionOps``
+- IRQ handling: ``qemu_irq``, ``qemu_set_irq()``
+- Properties: ``DEFINE_PROP_*`` macros
+- Module system: ``type_init()``, ``module_obj()``
+
+Unstable APIs (Use with caution)
+---------------------------------
+
+These APIs may change between QEMU versions:
+
+- Internal helper functions
+- Target-specific code
+- Device implementation details
+- Non-public headers
+
+Always rebuild device modules when updating QEMU.
+
+Debugging
+=========
+
+Enable Module Loading Traces
+-----------------------------
+
+::
+
+    qemu-system-x86_64 -trace 'module_*' -device mydevice
+
+Use GDB
+-------
+
+::
+
+    gdb --args qemu-system-x86_64 -device mydevice
+    (gdb) break my_device_realize
+    (gdb) run
+
+Check Module Symbols
+--------------------
+
+::
+
+    nm hw-mydevice.so | grep qemu_module
+    nm hw-mydevice.so | grep my_device
+
+Common Issues
+=============
+
+Module Not Found
+----------------
+
+**Problem**: ``Error: 'mydevice' is not a valid device``
+
+**Solutions**:
+
+- Check ``QEMU_MODULE_DIR`` is set correctly
+- Verify module filename matches: ``hw-<typename>.so``
+- Ensure module is in a directory QEMU searches
+
+Symbol Errors
+-------------
+
+**Problem**: ``undefined symbol`` errors when loading
+
+**Solutions**:
+
+- Ensure ``BUILD_DSO`` is defined
+- Link against GLib: ``$(pkg-config --libs glib-2.0)``
+- Check all required headers are included
+
+Version Mismatch
+----------------
+
+**Problem**: ``module version mismatch``
+
+**Solutions**:
+
+- Rebuild module against correct QEMU SDK version
+- Ensure SDK version matches installed QEMU version
+
+Advanced Topics
+===============
+
+Properties
+----------
+
+Add device properties::
+
+    static Property my_device_properties[] = {
+        DEFINE_PROP_UINT32("reg-size", MyDeviceState, reg_size, 0x1000),
+        DEFINE_PROP_STRING("name", MyDeviceState, name),
+        DEFINE_PROP_END_OF_LIST(),
+    };
+
+    static void my_device_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, const void *data)
+    {
+        DeviceClass *dc = DEVICE_CLASS(oc);
+        device_class_set_props(dc, my_device_properties);
+    }
+
+Character Device Backend
+------------------------
+
+Connect to character devices::
+
+    #include "chardev/char-fe.h"
+    
+    typedef struct {
+        DeviceState parent;
+        CharBackend chr;
+    } MyUartState;
+    
+    static Property my_uart_props[] = {
+        DEFINE_PROP_CHR("chardev", MyUartState, chr),
+        DEFINE_PROP_END_OF_LIST(),
+    };
+
+Examples
+========
+
+See the QEMU source tree for device examples:
+
+- ``hw/misc/edu.c`` - Educational PCI device
+- ``hw/misc/debugexit.c`` - Simple ISA device
+- ``hw/char/serial.c`` - Serial port device
+
+External examples:
+
+- https://github.com/fvutils/qemu-model-loader/tree/main/examples
